    "physicalPage": 3,
    "completePrintedNames": [],
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.duvalelections.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1644/2026-General-All-Races",
    "sourceBlock": "Duval County School District Ad \nValorem Millage Election   \n \nShall the Duval County School \nDistrict continue the current one (1) \nmill ad valorem millage for essential \noperating expenses, shared \nproportionately with charter schools, \nincluding compensating teachers, \nsecurity, and support staff; \npreserving academic programs, and \nprotecting arts, athletics, and student \nactivities beginning July 1, 2027, and \nending four (4) fiscal years later on \nJune 30, 2031, with annual reporting \nto ensure proper fiscal stewardship \nof these funds to the citizens of \nDuval County?  \n \nYes, for continuation \nNo, against continuation"
  }
